cim:ErpInventory a owl:Class;
                 rdfs:comment "Utility inventory-related information about an item or part (and not for description of the item and its attributes). It is used by ERP applications to enable the synchronization of Inventory data that exists on separate Item Master databases. This data is not the master data that describes the attributes of the item such as dimensions, weight, or unit of measure - it describes the item as it exists at a specific location."@en;
                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61968.ttl>;
                 rdfs:label "ErpInventory"@en;
                 rdfs:subClassOf cim:ErpIdentifiedObject;
                 cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61968.InfIEC61968.InfERPSupport";
                 cimdoc:packageTier "Informative".
cim:ErpInventory.status a owl:ObjectProperty;
                        rdfs:comment "The status"@en;
                        rdfs:domain cim:ErpInventory;
                        rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61968.ttl>;
                        rdfs:label "status"@en;
                        rdfs:range cim:Status.
cim:ErpInventoryCount a owl:Class;
                      rdfs:comment "This is related to Inventory physical counts organized by AssetModel. Note that a count of a type of asset can be accomplished by the association inherited by AssetModel (from Document) to Asset. It enables ERP applications to transfer an inventory count between ERP and the actual physical inventory location. This count may be a cycle count or a physical count."@en;
                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61968.ttl>;
                      rdfs:label "ErpInventoryCount"@en;
                      rdfs:subClassOf cim:ErpIdentifiedObject;
                      cimdoc:cimPackage "IEC61968.InfIEC61968.InfERPSupport";
                      cimdoc:packageTier "Informative".
