cim:OilAnalysisGasAnalogKind.equivalentTCGPercent a owl:NamedIndividual,
                                                    cim:OilAnalysisGasAnalogKind;
                                                  rdfs:comment "Equivalent Total Combustible Gas (ETCG) percent. An estimate, calculated from the dissolved-gas concentrations and the oil sample temperature, of what the TCG would be in a gas space in equilibrium with the oil. ETCG reflects what the TCG would be in air spaces near the oil."@en;
                                                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61968.ttl>;
                                                  rdfs:label "equivalentTCGPercent"@en;
                                                  cimdoc:enumCode 18 .
cim:OilAnalysisGasAnalogKind.estimatedSafeHandlingLimit a owl:NamedIndividual,
                                                          cim:OilAnalysisGasAnalogKind;
                                                        rdfs:comment "Estimated Safe Handling Limit (ESHL) (in percent). Estimated safe handling limit is an estimate of the lower flammability limit (LFL) of the combustible gas mixture which the dissolved gas in the oil would give off by the oil if exposed to air. Expressed in percent like the equivalent total combustible gas percent, it is calculated from the dissolved-gas concentrations, the oil sample temperature, and the lower flammability limits of the individual combustible gases."@en;
                                                        rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://cimbology.com/ontology/iec61968.ttl>;
                                                        rdfs:label "estimatedSafeHandlingLimit"@en;
                                                        cimdoc:enumCode 22 .
